---
name: NXLog Windows Event JSON → OCSF
description: |
  Read Windows Event Log records serialized as JSON by NXLog and normalize them
  to OCSF. With NXLog Enterprise Edition, configure `AddPrefix TRUE` to keep
  provider fields apart from NXLog metadata. NXLog Community Edition does not
  support `AddPrefix`: it delivers EventData fields flat, drops unnamed `<Data>`,
  `<Binary>`, and `UserData`, and overwrites EventData fields that share a name
  with NXLog fields, such as `ProcessId`, with NXLog's values.
---

from_file "nxlog.ndjson" {
  read_lines
}
event = line.parse_json(unflatten_separator=".")
microsoft::windows::ocsf::normalize event, into=ocsf
ocsf.metadata.log_format = "json"
ocsf.raw_data = move line
ocsf.raw_data_size = ocsf.raw_data.length_bytes()
this = ocsf_cast(ocsf_derive(ocsf))
